## Progress this session (build `C0BB2B4F`, deployed all 4 nodes)

Three root-cause fixes landed, each proven with RULE-4 instrumented evidence:

**FIX A — inode-reuse adopt** (`xfs_mxfs_dlm.c` ~2323): The `RELOAD-SIZE-DROP-SKIP` heuristic had no generation check, so under inode-number reuse it kept a stale prior incarnation and then unlinked/inactivated that ghost → bnobt double-free / AGI corruption. Gated the skip on `di_gen == in-core gen`. Proven via the ino=6291588 cross-node timeline.

**FIX B — P102 `!in_ail` restore** (`xfs_mxfs_dlm.c` ~4242): sess102's in_ail-discard conflated *commit* (clears DIRTY, sets IN_AIL, data still in-core) with *writeback* (pushes to SCST cache). It was discarding this node's own committed-but-not-destaged AGI unlinked-list adds. Proven decisively: `P82-ADD → P102 discards AGI daddr=2 → P71 head=NULL → shutdown`. Restoring `!in_ail` eliminated the AGI sig-3 corruption (P71=0).

**FIX C — modify-path dir cold-read** (new `mxfs_dlm_dir_modify_refresh`, wired into `xfs_remove`): sess97 only added the acquire-side dir refresh to the read path. The modify path RMW'd the shared dir block from a stale base, resurrecting peers' deleted dirents — the all-nodes-agree durable lost-update (all 4 nodes saw the same 35 leftover files). **unlink_visibility now PASSES in isolation.**

Also exposed a methodology flaw that had been polluting results: `reset4.sh` doesn't reboot, so dmesg persists and stale "Shutting down" lines read as false fresh shutdowns — must `dmesg -C` per run.

